  "@type": "AnalogicalMapping",
  "instance_name": "mapping_1",
  "label": "The man is mapped as 'me' in the text",
  "description": "The text 'thank you for allowing me into your country' and 'now we need to talk about the things that need to change around here to accommodate my beliefs' explicitly refers to 'me'. The visual material, the man with the beard and crossed arms, is presented as the entity being referred to as 'me'. The juxtaposition of the text and the visual material creates an analogical mapping where the man is identified as the speaker ('me') in the text. This mapping is reinforced by the confrontational posture and direct gaze, which align with the assertive tone of the text.",
